# Copy to ".env" and edit, then run `make prod`.
# These configure the PRODUCTION first-run bootstrap: on an empty database the
# backend creates one school + one administrator (role "principal", full access).
# They are ignored in demo mode and once any account already exists.

# REQUIRED to create the admin (leave empty = no admin created, DB stays empty):
BBC_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-strong-password

# Optional — sensible defaults shown:
BBC_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
BBC_ADMIN_NAME=Administrateur
BBC_SCHOOL_NAME=Mon établissement
BBC_SCHOOL_CODE=SCHOOL
BBC_YEAR_LABEL=2025-2026

# Strongly recommended in real deployments — a 256-bit base64 secret:
# BBC_JWT_SECRET=...
# Access JWT lifetime in minutes (default 480 = 8h school day). Silent refresh
# extends the session up to BBC_REFRESH_TOKEN_DAYS without re-login.
# BBC_ACCESS_TOKEN_MINUTES=480
# BBC_REFRESH_TOKEN_DAYS=7

# ---- Stockage objet (MinIO) ------------------------------------------------
# Les fichiers de la bibliotheque de ressources (PDF, Word, images) y sont
# stockes plutot qu'en base : un PDF par circulaire ferait enfler le pg_dump.
# ATTENTION : le volume MinIO n'est PAS dans le pg_dump — sauvegardez-le aussi.
# Le bucket est prive ; les octets ne sortent que par l'API, apres controle.
BBC_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=bbc-storage
BBC_STORAGE_SECRET_KEY=change-me-strong-storage-secret
BBC_STORAGE_BUCKET=bbc-sms

# ---- Server deployment (./deploy.sh) ---------------------------------------
# Host the server is reached on (a hostname OR a bare IP) — used for the cert
# CN/SAN. deploy.sh puts an IP in an IP: SAN entry automatically.
DOMAIN=62.169.26.178
# Public origin the browser uses (scheme + host + HTTPS port) — for CORS.
# In sslip.io mode (below) this is derived automatically; leave it commented out.
PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://62.169.26.178:20443

# sslip.io — give a bare-IP server a real DNS name without owning a domain.
# Set USE_SSLIP=1 and deploy.sh turns DOMAIN=62.169.26.178 into the hostname
# 62-169-26-178.sslip.io (which resolves back to the IP), issues a cert with a
# real DNS SAN, and points CORS at it. Browse https://62-169-26-178.sslip.io:20443.
# Leave PUBLIC_ORIGIN unset (comment it out) so it is computed for you.
USE_SSLIP=0
# Alternatively set DOMAIN directly to a *.sslip.io name and leave USE_SSLIP=0.

# ---- Domain deployment (./deploy-domain.sh) --------------------------------
# For a real owned domain instead of a bare IP: set DOMAIN to the hostname
# (e.g. bbcomplex.com) — its DNS A record must already point at this server.
# deploy-domain.sh then issues a trusted Let's Encrypt certificate (ports
# 80/443, no browser warning) instead of the self-signed one above.
# DOMAIN=bbcomplex.com
# LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Avoid spaces and the '#' character in values (or wrap them in quotes).
